The TypeScript adaptation computes each output sample from the saved history
and the current frame directly instead of keeping per-channel scratch frames,
writing in place from the last sample backwards; the arithmetic and clipping
order are unchanged. Instead of the format and layout conversion native inserts
implicitly, it refuses any input that is not stereo 44100 Hz, and it accepts
no options. The original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream
submodule.
